WHY THIS FONT. Hong Kong street name plates are set in Kai (楷書). A sans-serif
plate is legible and wrong in a project whose whole claim is that the city is
accurate. This face also carries Hong Kong's own glyph forms, from the Education
Bureau's 《香港小學學習字詞表》 (2007), rather than Taiwan's or the mainland's.

ATTRIBUTION IS REQUIRED AND IS NOT OPTIONAL. CC BY 4.0 obliges the credit to
travel with every distributed build, which means the in-game credits screen and
not only this file. That is the same obligation hard rule 6 already imposes for
the government data, and it is discharged in the same place.

MODIFICATION IS PERMITTED. Unlike the SIL Open Font License, CC BY 4.0 carries no
reserved font name, so a subset built for one region may keep the name provided
the attribution stands and the change is indicated. Nothing subsets it today; see
DECISIONS.md Q79 for why that was recorded rather than done.

COVERAGE IS CHECKED, NOT ASSUMED. tools/font_coverage.py asserts that every
character in every street name the pipeline publishes is either in this font or
in the display substitution table, and refuses one that is not. It is run by
hand, like the other graders in tools/. Wan Chai needs 166
distinct characters and this font covers 165 of them; the exception, and the
reason it is not fixed in the data, is Q79.
